\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Every model and remedy in both worlds.} Medians over the 12 worlds of each kind (four planning strengths, three seeds). Forecast: item-by-store RMSSE on the merchants' own plan in the held-out weeks. New plans: mean over the eight held-out plans of $|\log (\text  {predicted change}/\text  {true change})|$. Price choice: revenue given up by the regular-price move the model picks, \% of the best. Promotion choice: true lift missed by the promotions the model picks, \% of the best. Stock: summed absolute error of ordering to the forecast, over expected sales. Rows marked + change one thing in the row above them; all rows after the first in each model, and the split and shape rows, were added after the first results (Appendix~\ref {app:plan}).}}{6}{table.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:remedies}{{2}{6}{\textbf {Every model and remedy in both worlds.} Medians over the 12 worlds of each kind (four planning strengths, three seeds). Forecast: item-by-store RMSSE on the merchants' own plan in the held-out weeks. New plans: mean over the eight held-out plans of $|\log (\text {predicted change}/\text {true change})|$. Price choice: revenue given up by the regular-price move the model picks, \% of the best. Promotion choice: true lift missed by the promotions the model picks, \% of the best. Stock: summed absolute error of ordering to the forecast, over expected sales. Rows marked + change one thing in the row above them; all rows after the first in each model, and the split and shape rows, were added after the first results (Appendix~\ref {app:plan})}{table.caption.22}{}}
